 "body": "Refs KS-723 \u2014 https://linear.app/secuura/issue/KS-723\n\n`GET /api/anchors/tx/:txHash` has been routed since `services/anchoring/src/index.ts:1089` and answers `{ success: true, data: <one anchor> }`, but the published OpenAPI document did not declare it. An undeclared operation is invisible offline: the contract suites have nothing to generate against it and a change to its response shape breaks no test. It is now registered on the shared registry `anchoring.openapi.ts` populates on import, so `npm run generate-openapi` emits it. **No route and no handler is changed.**\n\n## NARROWING, not closing\n\nKS-723 covers the remaining ~157 routed-but-undocumented `/api` operations and this declares **one** of them. Stuart named **two** `/api/anchors` reads on the ticket at 2026-09-29T09:21:26Z as Platform-S hot-path reads. Only `GET /api/anchors/tx/{txHash}` is declared here.\n\nThe other, `GET /api/anchors/{id}` (`index.ts:827`), is **deliberately left out \u2014 not rejected** \u2014 because declaring it on this registry would make the gateway answer **405** to two live `POST` routes sharing the prefix. **KS-723 stays OPEN for it.**\n\nKam ruled this on card `secuura-ks723-whose-to-raise-1005` = **a**: *\"Ours: raise the anchors-tx PR (Refs KS-723) through the QA gate \u2026 The ticket stays open for the second endpoint.\"*\n\n## Test Evidence\n\n**Touched (5 files, +354/\u22120):**\n- `Blockchain/Dev/services/anchoring/src/anchoring.openapi.ts` \u2014 the registration (one hunk at `:406`)\n- `Blockchain/Dev/services/anchoring/src/__tests__/ks723-anchors-tx-lookup-is-declared.test.ts` \u2014 NEW, 5 cells\n- `Blockchain/Dev/docs/openapi/secuura-api.yaml` \u2014 **REGENERATED**, never pasted\n- both platform-k documents \u2014 block `16.` / a new last section, in this same commit (skill \u00a74)\n\n**RAN, at base `d784b613c81e` and head `a94ec8f6a2c6`:**\n- **Red-first, by assertion:** test section applied, product hunk absent \u2192 `rc 1, 3 failed / 2 passed of 5 EXECUTED`. Five cells executed, so an assertion red and **not a load failure**; each red carries a real `AssertionError`. The file's own two control cells are green at both ends, so the three reds discriminate. With the product hunk: `rc 0, 5 passed of 5`.\n- **anchoring unit suite, same binary (`vitest run`) both ends:** base `27 files / 357 tests, 1 failed` \u2192 head `28 files / 362 tests, 1 failed`. Delta exactly **+1 file / +5 tests, 0 NEW reds**. The one failure is `src/__tests__/threadTokenMint.test.ts` at **both** ends \u2014 the pre-existing `@lucid-evolution` red recorded at `BACKLOG.md:182` on develop. Not introduced here. The base reading was taken by reverting the two tracked files and moving the new test aside, then restoring and proving all three **byte-identical by sha256** before re-running.\n- **Spec regenerated:** `npm run generate-openapi` rc 0, **310 paths**; `secuura-api.yaml` **1,351,218 \u2192 1,354,452 bytes** by `wc -c`; `/api/anchors/tx/` **0 \u2192 1**. `npm run check:openapi` **rc 0** (406 example blocks resolve). **Drift control:** a one-byte YAML edit gives `rc 1 \u2014 CHECK FAIL: generated YAML differs from on-disk version`; restored `cmp`-identical and rc 0 again.\n- **Pathgate:** 6 assertions, 0 failed, the measured path set exactly the declared 5, with three internal controls firing; an inverted control (one declared path removed) returns FAIL naming the extra.\n- **\u00a74 timing:** `0` stated timings cover an anchoring unit suite at the base. Instrument: `/usr/bin/grep -c -i -E` over both platform-k docs at `d784b613c81e`, pattern `anchoring.*unit suite` \u2192 0 flow / 0 cheat. Must-hit controls in the same files: `auth` **89/81**, `anchoring` **18/19**, so the zeroes are measurements. No timing row amended, no tier budget moves.\n- Measured **2026-10-05**, host **Kamil's Mac Studio (2)**, node **v24.7.0**, under concurrent fleet load.\n\n**NOT RUN \u2014 and one of these is a green that does not mean what it looks like:**\n- \ud83d\udd34 **`tsc` is rc 0 but does NOT cover the new test file.** Its control fires on the product file (a planted `TS2322` in `anchoring.openapi.ts` \u2192 `rc 2`, restored byte-identical). But `services/anchoring/tsconfig.json` has `exclude: ['node_modules','dist','src/__tests__']`, so the new test is **not in the program** \u2014 0 occurrences under `--listFilesOnly`, and the same planted error *inside the test file* still gives rc 0. `anchoring` has no `typecheck` script and vitest transpiles without type-checking, so **the new test file is TYPE-UNCHECKED**. The tsconfig is deliberately not widened in this PR.\n- **The four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, k6) were NOT run.**\n- **No live sweep.** Nothing was exercised against a running stack: no gateway, no database.\n- **In-hook preflight, quoted exactly:** `PREFLIGHT INCOMPLETE \u2014 12/15 legs ran, 3 SKIPPED. Nothing failed.` / `legs 3 4 8 \u2014 local stack not up`. **12 of 15 is NOT a pass.** Alongside it: `shell suites: 67 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (of 67)` and `OK \u2014 13 code guards passed.`\n\n**Migrations + config:** none. No migration, no dependency, no lockfile, no manifest, no baseline, and no new pre-push leg (Kam's card `secuura-pushgate-three-legs-1005` = a, \"Add none of them now\").\n\n## NOT COVERED (skill \u00a75f)\n\nThis is a **runtime change** with **no live sweep**, so **KS-723 does not move to Done** on its account and stays open for the second endpoint. Two things are **UNMEASURED**: that the gateway actually serves the newly declared operation, and that the runtime response really matches the declared envelope \u2014 the cells read the generated document, not a live response.\n\n## For the merger\n\nBase is develop as read at boot, `d784b613c81e`. develop has since moved, so this needs a docs merge-in judged by the gate's own key-anchored predicted tree. **Use a newline-tolerant `<h2>` reader:** #1390 splits those tags, and my own flow-document reading was taken at `d784b613c81e`, which predates it. Placement as ruled: flow block `16.` between `14.` and `18.` (numbered `<h2>`s ascending, 17 total), cheat sheet a new **last** section after KS 1005.\n\nThe held carve for this change declares `@@ -406,7 +406,44 @@` and `git apply` refuses it `rc 128 corrupt patch at line 57`. Counting the hunk body \u2014 51 lines \u2014 gives old 7 (matching the shipped `-406,7`) and new **50**; the shipped 44 is short by 6. A header-fixed copy differing in exactly that one line was applied, and the held artefact was re-hashed afterwards unchanged.\n",
